    "teach_6": {
      "id": "teach_6",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "One exponent often surprises learners: zero.\n\nTake 6^4 ÷ 6^4. The number divided by itself is 1.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_6_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_6_step": {
      "id": "teach_6_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "But the quotient law also gives:\n\n6^4 ÷ 6^4 = 6^(4−4) = 6^0\n\nSo 6^0=1. For any non-zero base, exponent zero gives 1 — not 0.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_6"
        }
      ]
    },
